    "body": "Great on any Friday: CRAFTSMAN V20 - Tire Inflator, Portable Air Compressor\nCupra Launches ABT-Tuned Raval and Leon in the UK, Here's How Much the New Range-Toppers Cost\n9 photos\nPhoto: Cupra UK\nCupra and ABT Sportsline continue their collaboration by introducing modded versions of the Raval and the Leon in the United Kingdom.\nFollowing in the footsteps of the Cupra Formentor VZ ABT , which launched earlier this month (November 2026), the two models are called the Cupra Raval VZ ABT and the Leon VZ ABT.\nPricing starts from 36,995 pounds (equal to $48,430) for the Cupra Raval VZ ABT, which is said to be eligible for a 1,500 pounds ($1,965) ECG (Electric Car Grant) discount. As for the Leon VZ ABT, it starts at 48,510 pounds ($63,505) OTR, and it obviously sits at the top of the family, above the previous range-topper, namely the VZ, which kicks off at 45,370 pounds ($62,015) locally.\nLesser versions of the Cupra Leon (Hatch) include the Shadow Edition, V2, and V1, and these can be ordered from 37,540 pounds ($49,145), 34,475 pounds ($45,130), and 32,580 pounds ($42,650), respectively. As for the Raval lineup, it kicks off from 25,495 pounds ($32,065) for the V1, and also includes the V2, VZ, and VZ Extreme, priced from 28,080 pounds ($36,760), 34,495 pounds ($45,160), and 34,810 pounds ($45,570), respectively. The Raval Origin will join the family in 2027.\nPhoto: Cupra UK Announced during the Paris Motor Show earlier this year, the VZ ABT is pretty much a styling package that was developed in partnership between Cupra and ABT Sportsline. The automaker and the renowned tuner say that the bundle comprises several hand-fitted exterior enhancements. These include stuff such as the skirts at the front and rear, as well as the side skirt add-ons, a distinctive roof spoiler, and subtle winglets at both ends.\nNo tuning job would be complete these days without a set of aftermarket wheels, and the VZ ABT versions of the Cupra Raval and Leon also tick this box. The company says that the alloys of choice in this case are called the ICON. They measure 19 inches in diameter, are presented in matte black, and feature ABT branding on them in order to make them more recognizable.\nIt is definitely worth noting that each Custom Cupra by ABT pack is equipped by hand at the Cupra Racing Factory, and it is a great way to make your Raval or Leon, or the Formentor, for that matter, which starts at 54,125 pounds ($70,855) OTR in the United Kingdom. The latter comes with a 2-liter four-pot making 333 ps (328 hp/245 kW).\nCupra’s Formentor VZ5 ABT is also available in the UK, packing the Audi Sport-sourced 2.5-liter five-banger that develops 390 ps (385 hp/287 kW), and kicks off at 66,420 pounds ($86,950). The regular non-ABT Formentor also comes in the VZ5, VZ, V2, and V1 trim levels, and it starts at 64,495 pounds ($84,430), 48,455 pounds ($63,435), 37,875 pounds ($49,585), and 35,530 pounds ($46,515), respectively, the automaker’s official local website reveals.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nCupra Raval Cupra Leon Cupra raval Leon ABT Sportsline prices UK\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT Tesla Cybertruck Gets $5,000 More Expensive After the Latest Price Hike, and It Makes No Sense",
